Originally I didn't have a strong preference as to which way we take, but now looking at the API again from a high level, I do lean toward this approach:

``` ts
export interface TreeExplorerNodeProvider {
    provideRootNode(): TreeExplorerNode | Thenable<TreeExplorerNode>;
    resolveChildren(node: TreeExplorerNode): TreeExplorerNode[] | Thenable<TreeExplorerNode[]>;
}

export interface TreeExplorerNode {
    label: string;
    hasChildren?: boolean;
    onClickCommand?: Command;
}
```

In the extension, doing this:

``` ts
// Provider
getLabel(node: DepNode): string {
  switch (node.kind) {
    case 'root':
      return '';
    case 'node':
      return node.moduleName;
    case 'leaf':
      return node.moduleName;
  }
}
```

or this:

``` ts
class Root implements TreeExplorerNode {
  label: '';
}

class Node implements TreeExplorerNode {
  get label() { return this.moduleName; }
}

class Leaf {
  get label() { return this.moduleName; }
}
```

is more a matter of preference.

But I do observe a strong consistency in the API about the `registerSomethingProvider`, and then `Provider.provideSomething(): Something | Thenable<Something>`

``` ts
function registerCompletionItemProvider(selector: DocumentSelector, provider: CompletionItemProvider, ...triggerCharacters: string[]): Disposable;
function registerCodeActionsProvider(selector: DocumentSelector, provider: CodeActionProvider): Disposable;
function registerCodeLensProvider(selector: DocumentSelector, provider: CodeLensProvider): Disposable;

interface CompletionItemProvider {
  provideCompletionItems(document: TextDocument, position: Position, token: CancellationToken): CompletionItem[] | Thenable<CompletionItem[]> | CompletionList | Thenable<CompletionList>;
  resolveCompletionItem?(item: CompletionItem, token: CancellationToken): CompletionItem | Thenable<CompletionItem>;
}
interface CodeActionProvider {
  provideCodeActions(document: TextDocument, range: Range, context: CodeActionContext, token: CancellationToken): Command[] | Thenable<Command[]>;
}
interface CodeLensProvider {
  provideCodeLenses(document: TextDocument, token: CancellationToken): CodeLens[] | Thenable<CodeLens[]>;
  resolveCodeLens?(codeLens: CodeLens, token: CancellationToken): CodeLens | Thenable<CodeLens>;
}
```

and I'd rather not break that consistency.

